---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
// Written to describe what the public website actually does: a static site on GitHub Pages with self-hosted
// fonts, no cookies or browser storage, no analytics, no forms or accounts, and email as the only way to send
// information. Review this page whenever any of that changes.
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Digit Software handles information in connection with its website, digit.software."
  path="/privacy"
  updated="October 3, 2026"
>
  <section>
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how Digit Software ("Digit," "we," "us," or "our") handles information in
      connection with our website at <a href="https://digit.software/">digit.software</a> (the "Website"). It
      describes the information that may be associated with your use of the Website and what we do with information
      you choose to send us.
    </p>
    <p>
      This policy applies only to the Website. It does not cover other websites, products, or services, including
      third-party websites the Website may link to.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The Website does not use cookies, analytics, advertising, or tracking technologies.</li>
      <li>The Website has no forms, user accounts, or sign-in.</li>
      <li>If you email us, we receive the information you choose to send.</li>
      <li>Our hosting provider processes standard technical information in order to deliver the Website.</li>
      <li>We do not sell personal information.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Information You Provide</h2>
    <p>
      The Website does not include contact forms, account registration, newsletters, or any other way to submit
      information through the site itself. It lists an email address, <a href="mailto:info@digit.software">info@digit.software</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you email us, we receive the information you choose to include, such as your name, email address, company
      or organization, role, the contents of your message, and any attachments. Please avoid including sensitive
      personal information in emails to us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Information Associated with Website Access</h2>
    <p>
      When you visit the Website, your browser sends standard technical information to the servers that deliver it,
      such as your IP address, browser and device type, operating system, the page requested, the referring page, and
      the date and time of the request. This is a normal part of how websites work.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Website is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service provided by GitHub, Inc. GitHub processes this technical
      information to deliver the Website and to keep its service secure, and it may log visitor IP addresses for
      security purposes. GitHub handles that information under its own privacy statement.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not run analytics on the Website, and we do not use technical information about visits to identify
      individual visitors or to build profiles.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Cookies and Browser Storage</h2>
    <p>
      We do not set cookies on the Website, and the Website does not store information in your browser's local
      storage or session storage. It does not use tracking pixels, analytics scripts, advertising technologies, or
      similar tools.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your browser may keep its own ordinary cache of pages, fonts, and images so the Website loads faster. You can
      clear that cache in your browser settings at any time.
    </p>
    <p>
      Interactive elements on the Website run entirely in your browser. For example, text you type into the search
      field of the illustrative knowledge explorer on the Platform page is used only to filter the example records on
      that page. It is not sent to us or stored.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>
      The Website is a static website. Its pages, scripts, styles, fonts, and images are all served from the Website
      itself. We do not embed third-party analytics, advertising, social media widgets, video players, maps, or other
      third-party content.
    </p>
    <p>The service providers involved in operating the Website and handling your messages are:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Website hosting:</strong> GitHub Pages, provided by GitHub, Inc., which delivers the Website.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Email:</strong> the provider of our business email service, which receives and stores messages sent to
        info@digit.software.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>These providers process information as needed to provide their services, under their own terms and policies.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
    <p>We use information you send us to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>read and respond to your message;</li>
      <li>communicate with you about your inquiry, including follow-up about partnerships, business opportunities, or other topics you raise;</li>
      <li>keep appropriate records of our business correspondence;</li>
      <li>operate, maintain, and protect the Website, including against misuse and abuse; and</li>
      <li>comply with legal obligations and protect our legal rights.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not use information from the Website for advertising, and we do not use it to build profiles about visitors.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How Information May Be Shared</h2>
    <p>We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for advertising. We may share information only:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>with service providers that help us operate the Website and our business email, to the extent they need it to provide their services;</li>
      <li>
        when required by law, legal process, or a valid request from a public authority, or when reasonably necessary
        to protect the rights, property, or safety of Digit or others;
      </li>
      <li>
        in connection with a merger, acquisition, financing, reorganization, or sale of all or part of our business, in
        which case information may be transferred as part of that transaction; or
      </li>
      <li>with your consent or at your direction.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How Long We Keep Information</h2>
    <p>
      We keep correspondence for as long as reasonably necessary to respond to you, maintain business records,
      continue any discussion or relationship that follows, and meet legal, accounting, or security needs. When
      information is no longer needed for those purposes, we delete it or, where that is not practical, keep it
      securely until it can be deleted.
    </p>
    <p>Technical information processed by our hosting provider is kept under that provider's own policies.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use reasonable measures appropriate to a website of this kind, and the Website is served over an encrypted
      HTTPS connection. No method of transmitting or storing information is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee
      absolute security. Email is not always encrypted from end to end, so please keep this in mind before sending us
      anything confidential.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>External Links</h2>
    <p>
      The Website may link to websites and services operated by others. Those websites have their own privacy
      practices, and this policy does not apply to them. We are not responsible for how third parties handle
      information, so please review their privacy policies before sharing information with them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The Website is intended for a general business audience and is not directed to children under 13. We do not
      knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has sent us personal information,
      please contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your Choices and Requests</h2>
    <p>
      Because the Website does not use cookies, analytics, or accounts, there are no tracking settings to manage on
      the Website.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you have contacted us and would like to ask what information we hold about you, request a correction, or ask
      us to delete your correspondence, email <a href="mailto:info@digit.software">info@digit.software</a>. We will
      respond within a reasonable time.
    </p>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights under the privacy laws that apply to you, such as
      rights to access, correct, delete, or receive a copy of your personal information, or to object to or restrict
      certain uses of it. We will handle requests in line with the laws that apply. We may need to confirm your
      identity before acting on a request, and some requests may be limited where the law allows, for example where
      we must keep information for legal reasons.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Visitors Outside the United States</h2>
    <p>
      Digit is based in the United States, and our service providers may process information in the United States
      and other countries. If you use the Website or contact us from elsewhere, your information may be processed in
      countries whose data protection laws differ from those where you live.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy as the Website or our practices change. When we do, we will post the updated
      policy on this page and change the "Last updated" date at the top.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or requests about this Privacy Policy can be sent to:</p>
    <p class="contact-block">
      Digit Software<br />
      <a href="mailto:info@digit.software">info@digit.software</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
